{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Day 39 — Gradient boosting intro (XGBoost/LightGBM)\n","Objectives:\n","- Train a GBM model.\n","- Tune key params (learning_rate, n_estimators, max_depth).\n","- Overfitting/underfitting tradeoffs."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.datasets import load_breast_cancer\n","from xgboost import XGBClassifier\n","from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n","X,y = load_breast_cancer(return_X_y=True)\n","Xtr,Xte,ytr,yte = train_test_split(X,y,random_state=42)\n","xgb = XGBClassifier(n_estimators=300, learning_rate=0.05, max_depth=4, subsample=0.9, colsample_bytree=0.9, eval_metric='logloss', random_state=42)\n","xgb.fit(Xtr,ytr)\n","xgb.score(Xte,yte)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Exercises\n","1) Tune learning_rate and n_estimators with a simple loop.\n","2) Compare XGB vs LightGBM if installed."]}]}
